{
  "enum": "GameObjectActions",
  "description": "SpellEffect.EffectMiscValue_0 under effect 86, ACTIVATE_OBJECT -> what the spell does to the gameobject it reaches; EffectMiscValue_1 is the action's own parameter, an AnimKit id for 35 to 38 and a SpellVisual id for 42. Surfaced as the action word on an activation row; 0 is no action, shown as no word. The class says what a bare prop can answer: a model action asks the model for an animation and works on anything that has it, a state action needs a gameobject type with a state machine, and the rest are server bookkeeping. The client's own enum, transcribed by TrinityCore with the names lifted from the executable; too small and too free-form for read_enum_names, so it lives here.",
